@startuml emacs-layer
' The Emacs layer of Yeah: the person, the editor's Emacs, the agent's Emacs
' and the bridge between them.
'
' The editor's Emacs is the environment of the person: their packages, their
' configuration, their buffers.  The agent's Emacs is the harness: the kernel
' of the agent runs there.  The bridge is the only path from the harness to
' the live state of the editor's Emacs, and it is a capability the person
' approves on purpose -- not a scraping of files and process output.
'
' The wire of the placement carries the prompt and the answer of the person;
' the bridge carries the other way, from the harness to the live state.
'
' The six capabilities of the layer are the six points of the section of the
' site that this picture belongs to: BUFFERS, INTROSPECT, EDIT, DIAGNOSE,
' COMPOSE and RECOVER.  DIAGNOSE has two halves: the doctor the person runs
' in the editor and the diagnostics the agent calls in the harness.
'
' Every block that asserts something about the code names the files that
' implement it, as `file:line'.

package "drivers" as drivers {
  component "The person\nM-x yeah\nlib/yeah.el:37" as person
}

package "the editor's Emacs -- the environment of the person" as editor {
  component "BUFFERS\nlive buffers; unsaved edits are context\nlib/yeah-bridge.el:210" as buffers
  component "COMPOSE\nyour tools remain your tools\nlib/yeah-compose.el:83\nlib/yeah-compose.el:100" as compose
  component "DIAGNOSE\nno second build system\nlib/yeah-doctor-ui.el:148\nlib/yeah-emacs.el:152" as diagnose
  component "The approval view\nlib/yeah-approval-ui.el:43" as approval
}

package "the agent's Emacs -- the harness" as harness {
  component "The kernel\none turn of the agent\nlib/yeah-turn.el:1471" as kernel
  component "INTROSPECT\nthe runtime explains itself\nlib/yeah-emacs.el:62" as introspect
  component "EDIT\nchanges respect the buffer\nlib/yeah-diff.el:64\nlib/yeah-diff.el:105" as edit
  component "RECOVER\nhistory outlives the interface\nlib/yeah-session.el:167\nlib/yeah-org.el:94" as recover
  component "The bridge -- emacsclient\nlib/yeah-bridge.el:177" as bridge
}

note bottom of approval
  the human answers: :once, :session, :project, :global or :reject
end note

person --> compose : writes the prompt
compose --> kernel : the prompt
person --> approval : answers a request
approval --> kernel : the answer decides what may run
kernel --> bridge : the only path to the live state
bridge --> buffers : a capability you approve on purpose, not a default
kernel --> introspect : asks
kernel --> edit : previews a change
kernel --> recover : writes what happened
@enduml
